      "description": "This course provides an introduction to modern finance theory and its application to global financial markets. The course examines the foreign exchange market and related markets in derivatives such as foreign exchange futures, currency and interest rate swaps, and currency options, the eurocurrency market, international bond markets, and cross-border flow of equity investment.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "1. Pre-requisite(s): FINA2010 or FINA2310 or permission from the instructor\n2. Not for students who have taken FINA3010",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Lecture",
